# {{ stack }} stack

Generated by [kickinrad/stacks](https://github.com/kickinrad/stacks); `copier update` replaces this file. Record project exceptions in `AGENTS.md`.

## Base

- **Tasks:** mise is the only command authority. `mise run setup`, `check` (non-mutating gates), `test`; add `dev`, `e2e`, `build` only when they do real work. Stack defaults live in `.config/mise/conf.d/stack.toml`; override one by defining the same task in `mise.toml`.
- **Latest:** every tool and dependency tracks latest. Language lockfiles are committed and refreshed by Dependabot updates and `/stack update`; `mise.lock` is never committed. GitHub Actions are pinned by commit SHA (with the version in a comment) and Dependabot bumps them.
- **Instructions:** `AGENTS.md` only. No `CLAUDE.md`.
- **Git:** Conventional Commits; branch, pull request to `main`, squash merge. Lefthook runs `check` before commit and `test` before push. Never bypass hooks.
- **Secrets:** 1Password references and `op run`; never a secret in the repository. gitleaks scans every commit.
- **Owned files** (`STACK.md`, the checker, `.config/mise/conf.d/stack.toml`, CI, `.github/dependabot.yml`, workflow-lint configs) come from the template: change them upstream and run `copier update`. **Seeded files** start from the template and are then the project's to tune: `AGENTS.md`, `mise.toml`, `lefthook.yml`, `biome.jsonc` (keep extending Ultracite), `.mcp.json` and `.codex/config.toml` (keep the stack's servers), `.agents/project.toml` (the project's setup contract), manifests and sources. `.agents/stack/check` verifies the parts that must hold.
